# ADR

Path: `ADR/`. File name: `ADR-YYMMDDNN-slug.md`. The topic index of all ADRs is in the rule `adr-topics`.

| Topic | SSOT |
| ----- | ---- |
| When an ADR is necessary, file name, number `NN`, status, required sections | `playbook/principles/leveraging-adrs.md` |
| Branches, merge requests, rights of the CODEOWNER, replacement of an ADR | `playbook/workflow/adr-git-flow.md` |
| Template | `playbook/templates/adr.md` |
| Terms | `glossary/terms/adr.md`, `glossary/terms/architecture-decision.md`, `glossary/terms/architecture-solution.md` |
| Format of the discussion | `playbook/workflow/discussion-structure.md` |

Before you write a file, do these checks:

1. Find the highest `NN` for the date in `ADR/`. Add 1 to it.
2. Do not change the number or the file name after the creation of the file.
3. To replace an ADR, keep the file. Keep only the title and the status "Заменено" with a link to the new ADR.
4. Do not put links to specifications or code. These layers are lower.
5. When you add an ADR, add a row to the rule `.cursor/rules/adr-topics.mdc`.
